cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Oracle Provenance Is Invisible to Mutation Score: Agent-Generated Test
  Suites on Defects4J, With and Without the Implementation
message: >-
  If you use this data or these scripts, please cite the repository.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Parpal
    given-names: Sergi
repository-code: https://github.com/sergiparpal/mutation-study
abstract: >-
  Two test suites were generated per Defects4J bug with the same agent, model
  and instructions, varying only whether the agent could read the
  implementation. Over 36 bugs measured in both arms, real-fault detection
  falls from 72% to 14% while mutation score does not move (72% against 70%)
  and line coverage falls only from 85% to 73%. With an EvoSuite baseline over
  the same subjects, mutation score ranks the three suite populations in the
  wrong order. The repository holds the generation and measurement scripts,
  the per-suite measurements, a hand classification of the 40 faults, a probe
  of what the model recalls about each fault with no code in context, and two
  post-cutoff replication corpora.
keywords:
  - test generation
  - mutation testing
  - Defects4J
  - large language models
  - empirical software engineering
license: MIT
license-url: https://github.com/sergiparpal/mutation-study/blob/main/LICENSE
date-released: 2026-10-01
